{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/UniversityOfNotreDame/3743990015122816": {
      "title": "Salesforce Administrator & Business Analyst",
      "description": "The Salesforce Administrator & Business Analyst collaborates with functional teams to evaluate business objectives, user requirements, and process maps, delivering optimized technical solutions. The role manages end-to-end platform administration, security, and custom builds, while deploying automated workflows to streamline processes and minimize technical debt. Additionally, the position oversees solution testing, data health and governance, system documentation, and custom reporting/dashboards to ensure executive visibility into key adoption metrics. Serving as the primary point of contact for end-user support and enablement, the role executes continuous project delivery using Agile methodologies while integrating Salesforce release updates and industry best practices. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Application Configuration, Automation & Troubleshooting  Platform Maintenance & Security: Manage new and existing system features, including platform configuration, system maintenance, enhancements, upgrades, user management, and security configurations. Custom Declarative Build: Build and maintain custom objects, fields, record types, page layouts, and validation rules. Automation & Workflow Optimization: Design and deploy automated workflows using Salesforce Flow and Apex to streamline business processes while maximizing standard functionality and minimizing technical debt. Issue Analysis & Technical Support: Conduct analysis and technical support for application bug fixes, system troubleshooting, and solution validations. Requirements, Business Analysis, Design & Project Management  Business Objectives Alignment: Collaborate with functional team members to analyze business objectives, directions, and user requirements. Process Mapping & User Stories: Develop user stories and process maps to facilitate a shared understanding of business processes, system requirements, and design. Technical Solution Design: Recommend optimized business processes and technical solutions that deliver maximum return on investment to the organization. Quality Assurance, Data Governance & Documentation  Testing & Verification: Plan, develop, and execute solution testing strategies, user acceptance testing (UAT) criteria, test cases/scenarios, and manual/automated test scripts. Data Health & Governance: Oversee data health, hygiene, and governance, including duplicate management rules, data deduplication, mass imports/updates, and data backup procedures. System & Process Documentation: Author and maintain system and process documentation, including narratives and process maps, to support ongoing system utilization and maintenance. Business Practice Expertise, User Enablement & Agile Leadership  User Support & Enablement: Serve as the primary point of contact for internal user support, troubleshooting, and end-user enablement. Reporting & Analytics: Design, build, and maintain custom reports and dynamic dashboards for departmental and executive visibility, analyzing user adoption and key performance metrics to identify opportunities for process improvement. Best Practices & Release Updates: Maintain deep working knowledge of business processes, Salesforce release updates, and industry trends, collaborating with key customers and IT leadership to evaluate and share best practices. Agile & Scrum Execution: Lead and participate in Agile and Scrum work processes to drive continuous project delivery.   \n\n Minimum Qualifications 3+ years of hands-on experience in Salesforce platform administration, system configuration, and business analysis. Salesforce Certified Administrator. Technical Skills: Proven experience building complex automations using Salesforce Flow. Proficiency in managing user access, roles, profiles, permission sets, and security architecture. Experience writing detailed business requirements, user stories, and process maps using tools like Visio, Lucidchart, or similar. Hands-on experience with data management tools (e.g., Data Loader) and executing data hygiene/governance procedures. Methodology & Soft Skills: Experience working within an Agile/Scrum development framework. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills with the ability to bridge gaps between technical and non-technical stakeholders. ​​​​​​​Must be authorized to work in the United States without visa sponsorship. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Business Administration, or a related field (or equivalent combination of education and direct experience). ​​​​​​​Salesforce Certified Business Analyst, Salesforce Certified Advanced Administrator, or Certified ScrumMaster (CSM). ​​​​​​​Technical Skills: Basic understanding or light development experience with Apex and Lightning Web Components (LWC) to support declarative-first implementations. ​​​ Experience managing multi-cloud environments (e.g., Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud). ​​​​​​​Project Delivery: Demonstrated success in leading end-to-end UAT cycles, change management, and user adoption initiatives across business units. \n\n RESUME & COVER LETTER REQUIRED to be considered for this position. Please add in the attachments section of your application.  Salary:  $70,000 - $80,000, Commensurate with experience The University of Notre Dame seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administration. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or age in employment. Moreover, Notre Dame prohibits discrimination against veterans or disabled qualified individuals, and complies with 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-300.5(a). We strongly encourage applications from candidates attracted to a university with a Catholic identity.",
      "department": "Data/Analytics"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/UniversityOfNotreDame/3743990015122207": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "The University of Notre Dame Police Department (NDPD) is seeking highly motivated \nindividuals with excellent communication skills who want to work in a positive team \natmosphere. The campus is comparable to a small town with community members from \nall over the world. NDPD is a service organization that abides by the following values: \nRespect, Integrity, Service, and Excellence. We strive to provide superior customer \nservice and are community engagement-oriented. Come join a positive and diverse team \nworking collaboratively to create a safe environment for our students, faculty, staff, and \nvisitors. \n Currently Certified Law Enforcement Officers are preferred, however applicants \n meeting the minimum requirements will also be considered. \nThe Notre Dame Police Department is a full-service police department recognized by the \nState of Indiana with the authority to enforce Indiana State Laws, make arrests, and \nconduct criminal investigations. \n Details: Indiana Law Enforcement Academy is preferred or the equivalent Certified Officers will have an expedited hiring process Minimum Starting wage $31.50/hour Afternoon/night shift differential compensation Paid/Banked Holiday incentive compensation 4/3 10 hour work shift (1st shift 6am-4pm) (2nd shift 3pm-1am) (3rd shift 8pm-6am) Uniforms and equipment furnished Exciting paid overtime opportunities (Athletics, Concerts, Protection Details, Supplemental Shift Support and Training to name a few) Educational benefits to staff, spouses, and children 10% University gross wage contribution to 403b retirement fund Competitive medical, vision, and dental insurance plans (University contribution to \nHSA) On-campus comprehensive Wellness Center with lower co-pay options Current open position will likely be 3rd shift (8pm-6am) Specialty Divisions: Bike Patrol K9 Division Vapor Wake Comfort K9 Investigations Training Division Certified ILEA Instructors Field Training Officers R.A.D. (Rape Aggression Defense) Instructors Dignitary Protection Details Crime Prevention and Community Outreach Certified Drone Pilot Operators   \n\n Minimum Qualifications: 21 years of age High School Diploma or GED Valid vehicle Operator License Ability to communicate effectively with various constituencies Ability to supervise and adapt to rapidly changing situations, making appropriate \ndecisions under stressful circumstances Must maintain strong customer service focus even in difficult policing situations Must meet minimum standards regarding acceptance for training by the Indiana \nLaw Enforcement Training Board as specified in Indiana Administrative Code Title \n250 Rule 3 Preferred Qualifications: College Degree Tier I Certified Police Officer or the equivalent \n\n Starting Rate: $31.50/hr Applicants considered for hire will be required to participate in but not limited to \ninterviews, background investigations, psychological evaluations and drug screening. \nNon-certified applicants considered for hire will be required but not limited to the above \nincluding written comprehension testing as well as a physical agility test that mirrors the \nState of Indiana’s testing process. \nIf hired, non-certified persons will be required to attend and successfully pass the \nIndiana Law Enforcement Academy Tier 1 course. Check out additional benefit information  HERE ! The University of Notre Dame seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administration. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or age in employment. Moreover, Notre Dame prohibits discrimination against veterans or disabled qualified individuals, and complies with 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-300.5(a). We strongly encourage applications from candidates attracted to a university with a Catholic identity. \n\n The University of Notre Dame is more than a workplace; it is a vibrant, mission-driven community where every employee is valued and supported. Rooted in a tradition of excellence and inspired by our Catholic character, Notre Dame is committed to fostering an environment of care that nurtures the whole person—mind, body, and spirit. Here, you will find a deep sense of belonging, a culture that prioritizes well-being, and the opportunity to grow your career while being a force for good in the world. Whether contributing to world-class research, shaping the student experience, or supporting the University’s mission in other ways, you will be part of a dedicated team working to make a meaningful impact on campus and beyond. At Notre Dame, your work matters, and so do you!",
      "department": "Safety - Fire/Police"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/UniversityOfNotreDame/3743990015121546": {
      "title": "Cook 3 | Legends",
      "description": "The University of Notre Dame Operations, Events, and Safety  (UOES) division is currently hiring for a full-time Cook 3 in Legends in our campus Hospitality department. The UOES division oversees the University's event management, hospitality, and customer service functions, while also supporting student life, academic initiatives, research activities, and annual milestone celebrations.   Cook 3 Reporting to the Sous Chef, the Cook 3 is an advanced Back of the House (BOH) culinary position responsible for high-level food preparation, execution, and daily operational support within a high-volume ND Dining environment. This role operates with a high degree of independence and is expected to demonstrate strong culinary technique, consistency, and sound judgment. The Cook 3 provides day-to-day guidance to Cook 1 and Cook 2 team members, supports production flow, and helps maintain quality, safety, and sanitation standards. This position plays a key role in ensuring operational excellence and contributes to the development of the culinary team. Key Responsibilities: Execute advanced food preparation and cooking across multiple stations in accordance with standardized recipes and production schedules Maintain consistency in food quality, presentation, taste, and portioning Operate independently while supporting overall kitchen production and service execution Monitor station readiness, food levels, and service timing Provide informal leadership and daily guidance to Cook 1 and Cook 2 team members Assist in training new employees on recipes, techniques, and kitchen procedures Support production planning by organizing prep priorities and workflow Maintain strict adherence to food safety, sanitation, and HACCP standards Ensure proper labeling, storage, and rotation of all food products Maintain a clean, organized, and inspection-ready work environment Assist with inventory awareness, product usage, and communication of shortages Support waste reduction through proper handling and batch production Identify operational challenges and communicate effectively with the Sous Chef Contribute to recipe ingredient selection and consistent product execution \n\n High School Diploma or GED Progressive culinary experience in a commercial, institutional, or high-volume foodservice environment Demonstrated proficiency in multiple cooking techniques and station production Strong understanding of food safety and sanitation standards   \n\n Pay Rate: $19.50/hr The University of Notre Dame seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administration. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or age in employment. Moreover, Notre Dame prohibits discrimination against veterans or disabled qualified individuals, and complies with 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-300.5(a). We strongly encourage applications from candidates attracted to a university with a Catholic identity. \n\n The University of Notre Dame is more than a workplace; it is a vibrant, mission-driven community where every employee is valued and supported. Rooted in a tradition of excellence and inspired by our Catholic character, Notre Dame is committed to fostering an environment of care that nurtures the whole person—mind, body, and spirit. Here, you will find a deep sense of belonging, a culture that prioritizes well-being, and the opportunity to grow your career while being a force for good in the world. Whether contributing to world-class research, shaping the student experience, or supporting the University’s mission in other ways, you will be part of a dedicated team working to make a meaningful impact on campus and beyond. At Notre Dame, your work matters, and so do you!",
      "department": "Hospitality/Dining/Catering"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/UniversityOfNotreDame/3743990015120246": {
      "title": "Part-Time Monitor | Shields Athletic Dining Facility ",
      "description": "The  University of Notre Dame Operations, Events, and Safety  (UOES) division is currently hiring for a part-time Monitor in  Shields Athletic Dining Facility  in our Campus Dining department. The UOES division oversees the University's event management, hospitality, and customer service functions, while also supporting student life, academic initiatives, research activities, and annual milestone celebrations.  Monitor The  Monitor  welcomes guests and assists in supporting the mission and goals of a “Best in Class” dining program. This “front-of-house” position is critical to ensuring all diners feel welcome by providing a warm, friendly atmosphere and being responsive to the needs of our guests. This person is responsible for verifying student eligibility for meal service, monitoring overcrowding, preventing unauthorized individuals from entering or guests from exiting with excessive food, and maintaining cleanliness of the dining hall. Key Responsibilities: Greet and welcome students, faculty, staff, and guests upon entry to the dining hall in a friendly and professional manner Verify meal plans, student IDs, or other authorized access for all individuals entering the dining hall, ensuring proper entry protocols are followed Monitor dining room activity to maintain a safe, clean, and orderly environment, promptly addressing any spills, hazards, or disruptive behavior Circulate throughout the dining area, assisting patrons with general inquiries, directing them to different stations, or addressing minor concerns Ensure compliance with dining hall policies, such as \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"no outside food\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" or proper waste disposal, politely reminding patrons as needed Assist with maintaining the cleanliness of dining tables and chairs during service hours, wiping down surfaces as needed Report any equipment malfunctions, maintenance issues, or significant incidents to dining hall management immediately Support the overall dining experience by maintaining a visible and helpful presence, contributing to a positive atmosphere \n\n Capable of managing time effectively with minimal supervision Positive, respectful, and committed to the schedule you create Excellent communication and listening skills Ability to maintain a standing position for extended periods of time (up to 6 hours at a time). Follow food safety procedures for handling, storing, and serving food products \n\n Pay Rate: $17.50/hr The University of Notre Dame seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administration. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or age in employment. Moreover, Notre Dame prohibits discrimination against veterans or disabled qualified individuals, and complies with 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-300.5(a). We strongly encourage applications from candidates attracted to a university with a Catholic identity. \n\n The University of Notre Dame is more than a workplace; it is a vibrant, mission-driven community where every employee is valued and supported. Rooted in a tradition of excellence and inspired by our Catholic character, Notre Dame is committed to fostering an environment of care that nurtures the whole person—mind, body, and spirit. Here, you will find a deep sense of belonging, a culture that prioritizes well-being, and the opportunity to grow your career while being a force for good in the world. Whether contributing to world-class research, shaping the student experience, or supporting the University’s mission in other ways, you will be part of a dedicated team working to make a meaningful impact on campus and beyond. At Notre Dame, your work matters, and so do you!",
      "department": "Hospitality/Dining/Catering"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/UniversityOfNotreDame/3743990015112737": {
      "title": "Temporary | Tutor-CogSci Learning Design Team Leader (Literacy Focus)",
      "description": "Please apply through this link . Empower Tutors. Transform Literacy. Build Community. Are you a passionate leader driven to close educational opportunity gaps? Do you believe every child deserves access to high-quality, evidence-based literacy support? Join Tutor-CogSci as a Learning Design Team Leader . In this high-impact role, you will bridge cognitive science and real-world learning - coaching a team of dedicated tutors, partnering with local schools, and ensuring children receive the resources they need to thrive. Our Vision: To close educational opportunity gaps by expanding children’s access to high-quality, evidence-based literacy support aligned with the Science of Reading. Our Mission: We serve children, educators, and our community through three core pillars: Expanding Access: Delivering high-impact, evidence-based tutoring directly into local schools. Developing Future Leaders: Providing a premier practicum and workforce development experience for college students preparing for youth-serving careers (educators, pediatricians, cognitive scientists, and advocates). Innovating Learning Design: Advancing open science by developing, refining, and scaling effective tutoring practices.   Position Overview: As a Learning Design Team Leader , you are the heartbeat of our school-based operations. You will mentor, coach, and inspire a small team of tutors while fostering a vibrant, supportive community for both tutors and tutees. You’ll act as an exemplary representative of Notre Dame in the community, translating the Science of Reading into dynamic, daily practice. To keep your leadership grounded in real-world application, you will also spend a small portion of your time directly tutoring students using structured literacy programs. What You’ll Bring to the Role: Mentorship & Coaching: A passion for developing talent, delivering constructive feedback, and leading by example. Autonomy & Initiative: The drive to set goals, solve problems, and optimize your team's day-to-day operations. Relationship-Building: The ability to establish trust and strong partnerships across diverse groups—tutors, students, school staff, and university leadership. Note: You will receive robust onboarding in Tutor-CogSci’s methodologies and child safety protocols, along with ongoing access to leading literacy and math experts for consultation. Key Responsibilities: Team Leadership & Development: Manage, coach, and support a team of tutors delivering structured literacy programs to 2nd–3rd grade students. Modeling & Practice: Lead collaborative design meetings and model high-quality tutoring practices in action. Data-Driven Success: Track, analyze, and interpret tutor performance and student progress. Collaborate with Program Directors and Faculty Steering Committees to refine strategies and address learning trends. Community Partnership: Serve as a primary liaison between Notre Dame and school administration, fostering strong, transparent, and collaborative relationships. Cross-Functional Collaboration: Meet regularly with fellow Design Team Leaders and Assistant Directors to share best practices, optimize learning sequences, and solve challenges. Targeted Support: Monitor attendance and academic benchmarks, partnering with leadership to design tailored intervention plans for tutors or students who need extra support. Is This Role Right for You? This position is ideal if you: Are driven by purpose: You feel called to tackle educational inequities and hold high expectations for every learner. Love to mentor: You thrive on sharing knowledge, uplifting others, and helping team members realize their potential. Trust the science: You value educational research and actively seek evidence-based solutions to practical classroom challenges. Embrace continuous growth: You use feedback, data, and reflection to constantly refine your own leadership practice. Value connection & voice: You build authentic relationships, take a restorative approach to conflict, and view student voice as a vital asset in the learning process. \n\n Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in education or related field OR Bachelor’s degree with at least two years of exemplary experience directly relevant to our mission OR Associate’s degree with at least four years of exemplary experience directly relevant to our mission. Relevant experience includes working in a psychology or education research lab, experience working as classroom teacher, tutor, or coach; experience acquired while working as a student or raising children qualifies Highly organized and motivated to understand how children learn Demonstrates a “can do” attitude and comfort using technology Able to travel to schools in Goshen, IN Preferred Qualifications: Prior exemplary performance as a teacher, tutor, or mentor of students in a school or afterschool program; Lived experiences similar to those of the children we serve in Goshen; Experience working with children from a variety of racial, ethnic, linguistic, and socio-economic backgrounds;  Experience supervising, coaching, or mentoring others;  Experience teaching children using structured, evidence-based literacy approaches; Science of reading credential (please note: Indiana offers Keys To Literacy for Free to licensed Indiana educators, and we have resources to pay for others to take the Knowledge and Practice Examination for Effective Reading Instruction [KPEERI]) Experience working with and leading college students. \n\n The University of Notre Dame seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administration. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or age in employment. Moreover, Notre Dame prohibits discrimination against veterans or disabled qualified individuals, and complies with 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-300.5(a). We strongly encourage applications from candidates attracted to a university with a Catholic identity. \n\n The  University of Notre Dame  is more than a workplace! We are a vibrant, mission-driven community where every employee is valued and supported. Rooted in a tradition of excellence and inspired by our Catholic character, Notre Dame is committed to fostering an environment of care that nurtures the whole person—mind, body, and spirit. Here, you will find a deep sense of belonging, a culture that prioritizes well-being, and the opportunity to grow your career while being a force for good in the world. Whether contributing to world-class research, shaping the student experience, or supporting the University’s mission in other ways, you will be part of a dedicated team working to make a meaningful impact on campus and beyond. At Notre Dame, your work matters, and so do you!",
      "department": "Temporary"
    },
