    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/UniversityOfNotreDame/3743990015046546": {
      "title": "Department Coordinator | Art, Art History, & Design",
      "description": "The Department of Art, Art History, and Design is seeking an organized, proactive, and service-oriented Department Coordinator to support the department’s faculty, staff, students, and academic programs. The Department Coordinator provides administrative support to the Department Chair and faculty across studio art, art history, and design. The department includes approximately 20 full-time faculty, 4 concurrent faculty, and 10 staff members working across multiple campus locations. This position manages a broad range of departmental functions, including budgets and purchasing, faculty and student employment,  building operations, and academic program support. The role requires strong organization, attention to detail, sound judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities. Key Responsibilities Budget & Financial Administration Monitor and reconcile departmental accounts, expenses, and financial activity Process reimbursements, honoraria, check requisitions, and other payments Assist faculty and staff with budget systems, travel, purchasing, and related policies Prepare budget forecasts and the department’s annual non-regular budget submission Track funding and expenditures for BFA student awards Faculty & Personnel Administration Coordinate administrative processes related to faculty hiring, appointments, renewals, leaves, tenure, and promotion Support hiring of adjunct faculty and teaching scholars Coordinate visa-related processes for international faculty Maintain confidential personnel records and documentation Serve as a liaison with the Dean’s Office, Provost’s Office, and other university offices Department Operations & Purchasing Coordinate day-to-day departmental office operations Work with campus partners on building maintenance and service needs Purchase materials, equipment, and supplies for Studio Art and Design Coordinate purchasing needs for adjunct faculty and graduate students Manage departmental keys and building access needs Academic Program & Student Support Assist undergraduate and graduate students with registration, eForms, course overrides, and other academic processes Support administrative needs related to study abroad courses Maintain graduate student stipend information Assist with major advising coordination Provide administrative support for program meetings, student activities, and the annual graduation reception Student Employment & General Administrative Support Post student employment opportunities and process hiring requests Assist with student employee onboarding and approve hours Prepare reports, maintain records, and provide general administrative support to the department \n\n Required 1–2 years of administrative or related professional experience Strong organizational and time-management skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills Proficiency with Microsoft Office and ability to learn university administrative systems Strong attention to detail and accuracy Ability to manage multiple priorities and respond effectively to interruptions Professional, service-oriented approach when working with faculty, staff, students, and campus partners Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and solve routine problems Preferred Administrative experience in higher education or a similar environment Familiarity with university administrative, financial, or academic systems Experience supporting an academic department or multiple stakeholders Interest in or familiarity with art, art history, design, or related fields \n\n Application Deadline : September 18, 2026. Hiring Pay Range : Up to $23/hour. Required Application Materials : A resume and cover letter are required to be considered for this position. The University of Notre Dame seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administration. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or age in employment. Moreover, Notre Dame prohibits discrimination against veterans or disabled qualified individuals, and complies with 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-300.5(a). We strongly encourage applications from candidates attracted to a university with a Catholic identity. \n\n The University of Notre Dame is more than a workplace! We are a vibrant, mission-driven community where every employee is valued and supported. Rooted in a tradition of excellence and inspired by our Catholic character, Notre Dame is committed to fostering an environment of care that nurtures the whole person—mind, body, and spirit. Here, you will find a deep sense of belonging, a culture that prioritizes well-being, and the opportunity to grow your career while being a force for good in the world. Whether contributing to world-class research, shaping the student experience, or supporting the University’s mission in other ways, you will be part of a dedicated team working to make a meaningful impact on campus and beyond. At Notre Dame, your work matters, and so do you!",
      "department": "Office/Clerical"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/UniversityOfNotreDame/3743990015045356": {
      "title": "Part-Time Morris Inn Guest Service Associate (evenings)",
      "description": "The University of Notre Dame Operations, Events, and Safety  (UOES) division is currently hiring for a part-time  Guest Service Associate  within the  Morris Inn  in our campus Hospitality department. The UOES Division oversees the University's event management, hospitality, and customer service functions, while also supporting student life, academic initiatives, research activities, and annual milestone celebrations. The Morris Inn is a AAA Four Diamond Hotel and sits at the heart of Notre Dame’s storied campus. It continues to be the “living room” of the University of Notre Dame where guests will find the perfect atmosphere in which to enjoy a business lunch, family gathering, special occasion or a casual meal.  Guest Service Associate Are you a hospitality enthusiast with a knack for making people feel at home? The Morris Inn at the University of Notre Dame is excited to welcome a new Guest Service Associate to our team. In this role, you will be the first point of contact for our valued guests, providing personalized service, addressing their needs, and ensuring their stay exceeds expectations in our elegant and vibrant campus setting. Key Responsibilities: Greet guests when they arrive at the Morris Inn Check guests in/out of their stay  Answer questions and provide directions in a way that displays a high degree of hospitality Process hotel payments and post charges to guest folios Handle incoming and outgoing calls from guests and various campus departments *We are ideally looking for someone with evening availability. The shift is 3PM-11PM.*   \n\n Capable of managing time effectively with minimal supervision Excellent communication and listening skills Ability to maintain a standing position for extended periods of time (up to 6 hours at a time) \n\n Pay Rate: $17.50/hr The University of Notre Dame seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administration. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or age in employment. Moreover, Notre Dame prohibits discrimination against veterans or disabled qualified individuals, and complies with 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-300.5(a). We strongly encourage applications from candidates attracted to a university with a Catholic identity. \n\n The University of Notre Dame is more than a workplace; it is a vibrant, mission-driven community where every employee is valued and supported. Rooted in a tradition of excellence and inspired by our Catholic character, Notre Dame is committed to fostering an environment of care that nurtures the whole person—mind, body, and spirit. Here, you will find a deep sense of belonging, a culture that prioritizes well-being, and the opportunity to grow your career while being a force for good in the world. Whether contributing to world-class research, shaping the student experience, or supporting the University’s mission in other ways, you will be part of a dedicated team working to make a meaningful impact on campus and beyond. At Notre Dame, your work matters, and so do you!",
